{#
    The work list, shared by the home page's WORK section and the Work index so
    that the two cannot drift apart — including when the narrow-width layout
    changes how the gutter behaves.

    An organisation shows once per consecutive run. The comparison is against
    the previous item by index rather than a flag carried across iterations: a
    variable set inside a Nunjucks loop does not survive the loop frame, so a
    flag silently resets on every pass.

    The repeated ones are still written into the markup and hidden by class.
    Dropping them outright would leave a screen reader on the third Adobe item
    hearing a role with no employer attached, which is the one fact the gutter
    is there to carry.
#}
{% from "macros/gutter-list.njk" import entryRow %}

{% macro workList(items) %}
<ul class="gutter-grid">
    {%- for item in items %}
    {%- set repeated = loop.index0 > 0 and items[loop.index0 - 1].data.organisation == item.data.organisation %}
    {{ entryRow(item.data.organisation, item.data.title, item.data.summary, item.url, repeated) }}
    {%- endfor %}
</ul>
{% endmacro %}
